From: tarikbc <tarikbc@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 17:07:39 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Windows: anti-tamper stepping and fault delivery performance

Squashed from tarikbc/ageofempires-android patches 0004, 0006, 0009, 0012, 0013, 0014, 0017
(Age of Empires IV, Age of Empires II: DE). Reports the guest-visible protection of trapped pages,
makes raw x64 syscall return registers match Windows, skips the call-ret reset on invalidation
behind FEX_EXP_SKIP_CALLRET_RESET=1, compiles volatile code regions without faults or recompiles,
uses a 512 MB code buffer, reuses translations of re-decrypted code, and delivers guest faults
without a host trap (FEX_EXP_FASTTRAP=0 / FEX_EXP_FASTRAISE=0 turn it off).
Rebased onto 0001: two Core.cpp hunks and the RethrowGuestException hunk were placed by hand.
Left out: 0002 (hides the emulator), 0007 (rewrites ntdll export bytes), 0008 (debug tool),
0010 (obsolete on Proton 11.0-2), 0016 (hooks powrprof; belongs in Wine, bug 60462).

Upstream: FEX-Emu/FEX#6022 (0012/0014), #6023 (0004); 0006 reported as Wine bug 60461.
